# Google Sheets — `jobs` worksheet

Target worksheet name: **`jobs`** (never call it "Sheet A"). Downstream sheets are out of scope.

## Columns

`job_id` (string `{chat_id}_{message_id}`), `timestamp`, `url`, `crawl_status`, `job_title`, `job_description`, `job_location`, `job_company`, `job_salary`, `job_type`, `job_posted_date`.

## `crawl_status` values

`pending` | `running` | `finished` | `failed` | `rejected`

## Write rules

- Rejected/unsupported URLs still get a row with `crawl_status=rejected` — do not silently drop them after the chat reply.
- Use `gspread` + `google-auth` (service account). No hand-rolled Sheets HTTP.
- Batch and minimize writes — Sheets API has real rate limits; do not design around per-message synchronous writes.
